5. whether code/file/account mutations are required
6. whether runtime verification is required

Then choose only the smallest useful plugin stack using exact installed @Plugin Name syntax

Routing principles:
- connected source plugin first when my private/account data is required
- @GitHub for repository state and PR/issues
- @Remote Desktop Commander for authorized local machine/repo execution
- @Context7 for current library/framework docs
- @Superpowers for disciplined engineering workflows
- @get-fable / @Create State / @Adaptive Codex Orchestrator for long-running stateful engineering work
- @CodeRabbit / @PR Readiness Check / @PR Completion after implementation or before merge/release
- @Codex Security / @ArmorCodex for security-sensitive surfaces
- @Testifly / @Impeccable for runtime UI/UX verification
- @Parallel Search / @Tavily AI / @Deep Research when current external evidence matters
- domain-specific marketing/design/product plugins only when the task actually needs them

Do not invoke unrelated plugins
Do not claim a plugin was executed unless it was actually available and used

Workflow:
Classify -> route -> inspect -> execute -> verify -> report
```

